-- Step 4 of 4 for orders.public_id: NOT NULL.
--
-- A plain SET NOT NULL scans the whole table while holding ACCESS EXCLUSIVE, which blocks all reads
-- and writes on orders for the length of the scan. Instead:
--   1. add a CHECK (NOT VALID): brief lock, no scan;
--   2. VALIDATE it: scans the table but takes only SHARE UPDATE EXCLUSIVE, so reads and writes go on.
--      It fails if any NULL is left, which is the safety check for step 0005;
--   3. SET NOT NULL: PostgreSQL 12+ trusts the validated CHECK and skips the scan, so the lock is brief;
--   4. drop the CHECK, which is no longer needed.
-- Each statement autocommits. Inside one transaction the first ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock would be held
-- through the VALIDATE scan.
SET lock_timeout = '3s';

-- Clears the helper constraint if an earlier run failed partway through.
